---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../components/AdSlot.astro';
import { currentMonthYear } from '../utils/site-date';
import AppealLetter from '../components/AppealLetter.astro';
import AirportSidebar from '../components/AirportSidebar.astro';

const title = "Appeal Your Gatwick Airport Drop-Off Charge | Free PCN Appeal Letter 2026";
const description = "Got a parking charge notice for dropping off at Gatwick? Use our free appeal letter template to challenge your Gatwick PCN. Covers North and South Terminal.";
const canonical = "https://appealairportpcn.co.uk/gatwick-drop-off-charge-appeal/";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "How to Appeal a Gatwick Airport Drop-Off Charge",
  "description": "Step-by-step guide and free appeal letter for challenging a Gatwick Airport drop-off PCN, covering both North and South Terminal.",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealPCN" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealAirportPCN.co.uk" },
};

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much is the Gatwick Airport drop-off charge?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Gatwick currently charges £5 for a standard drop-off, enforced via ANPR cameras at both North and South Terminal." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I appeal a Gatwick drop-off charge?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Gatwick's drop-off charges are issued by a private parking company, not the council. You have 28 days to submit a formal appeal. If that appeal is rejected you can escalate to POPLA for free." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does the Gatwick drop-off charge apply to both terminals?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, both the North and South Terminal at Gatwick have dedicated drop-off charge zones, each enforced by ANPR cameras. The boundaries and signage differ slightly between the two." }
    },
  ],
};

const tips = [
  { heading: '28-day deadline', body: "Don't miss it, after 28 days you lose the formal right to appeal at the first stage." },
  { heading: 'Specify your terminal', body: 'Always state North or South Terminal in your appeal. The zones and signage differ between them.' },
  { heading: 'Request ANPR images', body: 'Ask for the entry and exit photos in your letter. Timing errors are common and hard for operators to defend.' },
  { heading: 'POPLA is free', body: "If rejected, always escalate to POPLA before considering payment. It costs you nothing." },
  { heading: 'Send by tracked post', body: "Proof of delivery matters if the case escalates." },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  currentPage="gatwick"
  schema={[articleSchema, faqSchema]}
>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <div class="wrap"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/gatwick-drop-off-charge-appeal/">Gatwick</a></div>
      </nav>
      <h1>Appeal Your Gatwick Airport Drop-Off Charge</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Charged for dropping someone off at Gatwick's North or South Terminal? You may have strong grounds to appeal, and our free template takes the guesswork out of the process.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap"><AdSlot type="leaderboard" /></div>

  <main>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="main-content">
        <div class="content-grid">

          <AirportSidebar current="Gatwick Airport" tips={tips} />

          <div class="airport-main-column">
            <AppealLetter airport="Gatwick Airport">
              <p>I am the registered keeper of the vehicle. I am not obliged to identify the driver and decline to do so.</p>
              <p>1. NCP cannot hold a registered keeper liable for any alleged contravention on land that is under statutory control. Gatwick Airport is not 'relevant land' as defined in Schedule 4 to the Protection of Freedoms Act 2012 ("POFA"). NCP is well aware that the POFA keeper liability provisions do not apply here, and has no lawful basis on which to pursue the registered keeper.</p>
              <p>2. NCP's 'parking charge' is not and never purports to be a byelaws penalty, it is a charge created for NCP's own commercial profit. If Gatwick Airport wished to enforce against vehicle owners or keepers under Airport Byelaws, that would be a matter for the landowner alone. NCP is not the airport owner and has no standing to invoke byelaws. Its claim rests solely on alleged breach of contract against the driver, not the keeper.</p>
              <p>3. The parking charge is not notified until after the contract is entered into. Under the Court of Appeal's decision in Thornton v Shoe Lane Parking [1971] 2 QB 163, a charge introduced after a contract has been formed does not become part of that contract.</p>
              <p>4. The signage is not compliant with the BPA Code of Practice. Charging terms were not displayed clearly or prominently before the driver committed to entering the zone, meaning no valid contractual offer was made.</p>
              <p>5. The vehicle was present in the drop-off zone for no more than 5 minutes, within the consideration period mandated by the BPA Code of Practice.</p>
              <p>The registered keeper cannot be presumed or inferred to have been the driver, nor pursued under any interpretation of agency law. NCP's Notice to Keeper can only hold the driver liable, and that claim also fails for the reasons above. I require this PCN to be cancelled and invite confirmation of cancellation in writing.</p>
            </AppealLetter>

            <div class="instructions-card">
              <h2>How to use this appeal template</h2>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-text">Click <strong>"Copy template"</strong> above, the full appeal is copied to your clipboard.</div></div>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-text">Log into the operator's online appeal system (or open your PCN) and paste the template into the appeal text box.</div></div>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-text">Submit and wait for a decision. The operator must respond within 35 days.</div></div>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-text">If rejected, request your POPLA code and escalate to the free, independent adjudicator, operators lose the vast majority of cases on these grounds.</div></div>
            </div>

            <div class="airport-info-panel">
            <section class="intro-section">
              <h2>Gatwick drop-off charge appeal</h2>
              <p>Got a PCN for dropping someone off at Gatwick? Use the free template above. It covers both terminals.</p>

              <h3>The charge</h3>
              <p>Gatwick has a drop-off zone at both the North Terminal and South Terminal.</p>
              <p>Cameras record vehicles entering the zones.</p>
              <p>The charge is <strong>£10</strong> for 10 minutes. After 10 minutes, it is <strong>£1</strong> for each additional minute up to 20 minutes.</p>
              <p>The maximum charge is <strong>£30</strong>. The maximum stay is <strong>30 minutes</strong>.</p>
              <p>You must pay by midnight the day after your visit.</p>
              <p>If you do not pay, Gatwick can issue a Parking Charge Notice.</p>
              <p>This is a <strong>private parking charge</strong>. It is not a council fine.</p>

              <h3>Why you can appeal</h3>
              <p>Gatwick's airport bylaws regulate the airport's land, buildings and roads. This can affect whether the Protection of Freedoms Act 2012 can be used to hold the keeper liable.</p>
              <p>You do not need to name who was driving, nor do they have any right to ask. This means that they cannot enforce keeper liability, as they can only confirm that you're the owner of the vehicle - <strong>not the driver.</strong></p>
              <p>Other points can help:</p>

              <ul>
                <li><strong>The zone boundary.</strong> Check the ANPR photos and the location of the drop-off zone.</li>
                <li><strong>Exit queues.</strong> If traffic kept you in the zone longer than expected, explain what happened.</li>
                <li><strong>Signs.</strong> Check whether the charge and its terms were clear before you entered.</li>
                <li><strong>Late payment notice.</strong> Check the date of your visit and the date of the PCN.</li>
                <li><strong>ANPR errors.</strong> Ask for the photos if the recorded times look wrong.</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="faq-section">
              <h2>Questions</h2>

              <details>
                <summary>Does the charge apply to both Gatwick terminals?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Gatwick has designated drop-off zones at both terminals.</p></div>
              </details>
              <details>
                <summary>How much is the charge?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>It is £10 for 10 minutes, then £1 for each additional minute up to 20 minutes. The maximum charge is £30 and the maximum stay is 30 minutes.</p></div>
              </details>
              <details>
                <summary>I was only there for two minutes, do I still have to pay?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Gatwick has a minimum £10 charge for using the designated drop-off zones.</p></div>
              </details>
              <details>
                <summary>Can I appeal if I didn't read the signs?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>You can appeal. The parking charge is not notified until after the contract is entered into. A charge introduced after a contract has been formed does not become part of that contract. The signage is also not compliant with the BPA Code of Practice.</p></div>
              </details>
              <details>
                <summary>What happens if Gatwick's operator rejects my appeal?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>This is unlikely. If it happens, check your rejection letter. If it gives you a POPLA verification code, you can make a free second-stage appeal.</p></div>
              </details>
              <details>
                <summary>Is the drop-off charge the same as a council parking ticket?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>No. It is a private parking charge.</p></div>
              </details>
            </section>

            <section class="grounds-section">
              <h2>Quick tips</h2>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Check the deadline.</strong> Use the date on your PCN. Don't miss your chance to appeal.</li>
                <li><strong>Name the terminal.</strong> Say whether you used North or South Terminal.</li>
                <li><strong>Keep proof.</strong> Save your appeal and any reply.</li>
                <li><strong>Keep copies.</strong> Save the PCN, photos and correspondence.</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="grounds-section sources-section">
              <h2>Sources</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Gatwick, <strong>Drop-off Charges</strong>: <a href="https://www.gatwickairport.com/transport-options/drop-off.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.gatwickairport.com/transport-options/drop-off.html</a></li>
                <li>Gatwick, <strong>Drop-off Terms and Conditions</strong>: <a href="https://www.gatwickairport.com/transport-options/drop-off/drop-off-terms-and-conditions.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.gatwickairport.com/transport-options/drop-off/drop-off-terms-and-conditions.html</a></li>
                <li>Gatwick, <strong>Regulation and Byelaws</strong>: <a href="https://www.gatwickairport.com/company/about-us/regulation.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.gatwickairport.com/company/about-us/regulation.html</a></li>
                <li>Protection of Freedoms Act 2012, <strong>Schedule 4</strong>: <a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/9/schedule/4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/9/schedule/4</a></li>
                <li>POPLA, <strong>Appeal guide</strong>: <a href="https://www.popla.co.uk/appeal-guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.popla.co.uk/appeal-guide</a></li>
                <li>GOV.UK, <strong>CCJs and your credit rating</strong>: <a href="https://www.gov.uk/county-court-judgments-ccj-for-debt/ccjs-and-your-credit-rating" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.gov.uk/county-court-judgments-ccj-for-debt/ccjs-and-your-credit-rating</a></li>
              </ul>
              <p>Gatwick's current published tariff is <strong>£10 for 10 minutes</strong>, then <strong>£1 per additional minute up to 20 minutes</strong>. The maximum charge is <strong>£30</strong>.</p>
            </section>

            </div>

            <div class="disclaimer">
              <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> AppealAirportPCN.co.uk is a free information resource for UK drivers. Nothing on this site constitutes legal advice. Templates are provided as a starting point, always review your specific circumstances. For complex cases, consider consulting a solicitor or Citizens Advice.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

</BaseLayout>
